# sway config for claude-display2-sway.service, the headless display that
# Claude Desktop computer use draws on.
#
# This file replaces sway's default config on purpose. The default config
# includes /etc/sway/config.d, whose systemd snippet sets XDG_CURRENT_DESKTOP
# to sway and imports it, with this sway's DISPLAY, SWAYSOCK, and
# WAYLAND_DISPLAY, into the session's user manager and D-Bus activation
# environment, and its bar block starts swaybar. tests/claude-display2-sway.zsh
# allows only the two directives below: nothing here may include files or
# start programs.
xwayland disable
# 1600x900 matches Claude Desktop's display presets.
output * resolution 1600x900
